tmosphere, despite communication difficulty.\n\nWe need to use explicit facts: B can be uncooperative; C creates a positive atmosphere with his crew; C is 100% reliable; C can make correct decisions quickly.\n\nThus we can argue that C's strengths in reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere outweigh B's cooperation concerns.\n\nThus we may change vote to Candidate C.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I appreciate the points about B, but I'm less convinced because B's uncooperative behavior is a serious safety concern. In contrast, C is known to be 100% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, and can make correct decisions quickly. These align with reliability, crew cooperation, and decision quality. Therefore I would shift my recommendation to Candidate C.\"\n\nMake sure to include metadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
